{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/88345-demons-in-the-underworld","id":88345,"title":"Demons in the Underworld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-10T12:12:02-07:00","id":88345,"title":"Demons in the Underworld","content":"So since the a Book of the Dead already came out, were probably not going to get any info on how Demons are affected by the Underworld. Given what we know do you think Demons would just be affected like a mortal? What additional problems might they have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T05:12:56-07:00","id":89402,"title":"","content":"I would personally treat them as per Promethean section on a failed Spoofing roll, and a regular mortal on a successful one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:46:12-07:00","id":1067741,"title":"","content":"Wow - I'm necroing this thread xD.<br /> <br /> So basically - I'm playing a crossover game with various splats, and one of the PCs is an Unchained Demon. Currently, the party has descended into the depths of the Underworld. My question and concern is how it affects them; are they able to go into full transformation without little penalties? Do ghosts/underworld beings fall subject to the same rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:11:07-07:00","id":1067755,"title":"","content":"Ok, I might not know the exact rules for how the Unchained handle the Old Laws and exactly how their Quantum Existence translates to the Underworld, but I know without a doubt that the Underworld is riddled with Infrastructure and agents of the God Machine. I'd say Cover worked exactly like it normally would, and a Demon who doesn't act in character risks drawing the attention of any Angels who are stationed in the Underworld. (For further verification, just look at the Ephemeral Entities section of DtD under Ghosts.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:25:07-07:00","id":1067764,"title":"","content":"Wew, things have changed since I made this thread.<br /> <br /> Very possible that Geist 2e could facilitate receiving an answer to this question at some point in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:54:50-07:00","id":1067846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/88345-demons-in-the-underworld?p=1067755#post1067755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(For further verification, just look at the Ephemeral Entities section of DtD under Ghosts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give a page number, because I'm looking in that section and not seeing anything about infrastructure in the underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:39:19-07:00","id":1067864,"title":"","content":"Most of the information about the Unchained in he Underworld can be found in the Storyteller's guide, actually. There is infrastructure there, but the God-Machine considers it &quot;damaged beyond repair&quot; and thus doesn't go into the deeper portions. As for whether the laws consider Demons humans, dead or other, I'd go with MCN's response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T02:11:18-07:00","id":1067951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/88345-demons-in-the-underworld?p=1067846#post1067846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give a page number, because I'm looking in that section and not seeing anything about infrastructure in the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I think I miss-quoted. I could have sworn there was an explanation of how the God Machine utilizes Ghosts and the Underworld in the write up for Ghosts in DtD, it might be earlier in the he book then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:34:49-07:00","id":1068100,"title":"","content":"So I see things somewhat differently. I feel like the nature of Demons is such that they can convince the Underworld to treat them as Mortals if they so desire and have a Cover available to create that illusion (I mean, convincing otherwordly and alien intelligences that they are perfectly normal human beings going about perfectly normal human being things is basically what Demons do 24/7 anyway). I might put them at risk of losing Cover if they brush up against an Old Law that applies to mortals (on the basis that whether they break it or not they will have come under close scrutiny by the entities that uphold such things for a few moments or two at least).<br /> <br /> Also, a Demon that goes loud faces similar problems to a Promethean in that the underworld doesn't necessarily know what to do with them. The difference is that there is an added danger in my mind. I would say that on a botch the Kerberoi or the Dominion interpret the connection between Demon and God-Machine to be as a manifestation of a rival Kerberoi (one that adheres to a particularly strange and distant order of Old Laws alien to the Dominion) attempting to invade or violate the Dominion's territory. A Demon so exposed risks being driven out of the Dominion, outright destroyed by an army of ghosts and the Kerberoi itself, or otherwise punished in whatever ancient and terrible manner one Kerberoi punishes another in the rare event of transgression. My rationale here is that just as some demons draw parallels to the Old Laws and Occult Matrixes so too might the rulers of the underworld look at the entities created to serve specific functions of this alien god and decide that the best way to treat them is the same as they treat their fellow Kerberoi and their servants.<br /> <br /> While I'm at it, what would you think of allowing the Demons to do a similar thing to vampires who learn to feed off of ghosts and allow a Demon who repurposes his systems to collect &quot;Ghost Dross&quot; in a similar manner to how they can usually collect &quot;Angel Dross&quot;? I doubt the essence of ghosts is completely interchangeable to that of Angels, but I figure they have as much if not more in common than mortal blood and ghost plasm. I'd of course make life as hard for a Demon who did this and later tried to acquire normal Aether in the real world as a ghost eating vampire who then wants to start sucking blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}